  "rootCause": "Crypto deposits and withdrawals frozen as BTCTurk faces Groundhog Day - $55 million lost in June 2024’s private key breach, now $51.7 million gone again, funds funneled into ETH, founder silent, and users are left watching the rerun.",
  "descriptions": [
    {
      "source": "REKT",
      "text": "Crypto deposits and withdrawals frozen as BTCTurk faces Groundhog Day - $55 million lost in June 2024’s private key breach, now $51.7 million gone again, funds funneled into ETH, founder silent, and users are left watching the rerun."
    },
    {
      "source": "DeFiHackLabs explorer",
      "text": "The Turkish cryptocurrency exchange BtcTurk suffered a compromise of the private keys controlling its multi-chain hot wallets on August 14, 2025. Unauthorized actors obtained credentials for wallets holding assets across Ethereum, Avalanche, Arbitrum, Optimism, Base, Polygon, Mantle, and Moonbeam, draining approximately $49M in total — with over $34M concentrated in two Ethereum wallets holding ETH and Layer 2 tokens. The attacker used MetaMask to rapidly swap multi-chain holdings to ETH for consolidation, then bridged and routed funds across chains to obscure tracing; a pre-established Solana wallet (created 56 days prior) was used for further laundering of memecoin-swapped proceeds. Private keys for multiple accounts appear to have been stored in the same location, allowing access to all hot wallets once one credential was obtained. BtcTurk replenished user balances from insurance and corporate reserves, restored operations within five days, launched a $2.4M recovery bounty program, and shared forensic data with Interpol — but this was notably the exchange's second multi-million-dollar hot wallet compromise within 14 months. Attack Tx: 0x0a08edc9e50b8212b0dcf831627b768a12b5e1ca573762e770fd3ba115ee85b2 Analysis: Halborn — Explained: The BtcTurk Hack (August 2025)"
    },
    {
      "source": "SlowMist",
      "text": "The Turkish cryptocurrency exchange BtcTurk has reportedly suffered another hack. BtcTurk acknowledged “unusual activity” in its hot wallets and has suspended deposits and withdrawals. However, the exchange did not disclose further details regarding the scale of the attack."
    },
    {
      "source": "RevertIQ",
      "text": "On August 14, 2025, BtcTurk's hot wallet infrastructure was compromised. Attackers stole approximately $48 million across seven blockchain networks by rapidly transferring and swapping assets from multiple hot wallets, prompting an immediate suspension of crypto deposits and withdrawals. Attackers obtained privileged access to the private keys controlling BtcTurk's hot wallets. This allowed them to execute unauthorized withdrawals across several chains. The exact method of key compromise (phishing, malware, insider involvement) was not publicly disclosed."
    }
  ],
